  "slug": "machine-prediction-fde3",
  "summary": "New preprints define Virtual Cell Challenge metrics and model non-additive effects and label noise in siRNA, combinatorial, and CRISPRi fitness prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is predicting responses to genetic perturbation while making evaluation, interaction structure, and label reliability explicit. The Virtual Cell Challenge 2026 specifies six metrics for zero-shot prediction of transcriptional responses to CRISPRi knockdowns. GAIN models single-cell combinatorial responses as an additive baseline plus a learned interaction term. siGMA applies a heteroscedastic multimodal model to chemically modified siRNA efficacy, quantifying uncertainty across noisy cross-dataset labels. FluxStack couples enzyme-constrained flux landscapes with light-aware knockdown FBA to predict light-dependent CRISPRi gene fitness in Synechocystis PCC 6803, a mechanistic counterpart to the data-driven models. BioSensor-X, a coverage-aware evidence-integration framework for E. coli transcription-factor prioritization, is more peripheral but shares the emphasis on explicit handling of uneven evidence.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
